# ---- heuristics for the CLRP
add('tuzun99', 'Tüzün, D., Burke, L. I.', 1999, 'A two-phase tabu search approach to the location routing problem', 'European Journal of Operational Research 116(1):87–99', '10.1016/s0377-2217(98)00107-6', 'heur', 'Two-phase tabu search; source of the T instance set.')
add('prins06a', 'Prins, C., Prodhon, C., Wolfler Calvo, R.', 2006, 'Solving the capacitated location-routing problem by a GRASP complemented by a learning process and a path relinking', '4OR 4(3):221–238', '10.1007/s10288-006-0001-9', 'heur', 'GRASP with learning and path relinking; source of the P instance set; local search with MOVE, SWAP and OPT moves.')
add('prins06b', 'Prins, C., Prodhon, C., Wolfler Calvo, R.', 2006, 'A memetic algorithm with population management (MA|PM) for the capacitated location-routing problem', 'Evolutionary Computation in Combinatorial Optimization (EvoCOP 2006), LNCS 3906:183–194', '10.1007/11730095_16', 'heur', 'MA|PM: chromosome = depot-status vector plus customer sequence cut into routes by Split; one-point crossover with repair; offspring are accepted only if their distance to the population exceeds a threshold. Local search LS1 (MOVE, SWAP, OPT, first improvement) or a light LS2 without moves between routes of different depots; a depot can be opened only by the crossover. Sets P, T and B (Barreto); one run per instance. Rounding of distances and code availability not stated; conclusion says the method is not yet definitively tuned.', read=True)
add('prins07', 'Prins, C., Prodhon, C., Ruiz, A., Soriano, P., Wolfler Calvo, R.', 2007, 'Solving the capacitated location-routing problem by a cooperative Lagrangean relaxation-granular tabu search heuristic', 'Transportation Science 41(4):470–483', '10.1287/trsc.1060.0187', 'heur', 'LRGTS: Lagrangean relaxation for the depot phase, granular tabu search (single-node transfer) for the routing phase, then a first-improvement local search with MOVE, SWAP and OPT (2-opt within a route or between routes). Creators of the P set: states that the P distances are multiplied by 100 and rounded up, and that B and T distances are not rounded.', read=True)
add('duhamel10', 'Duhamel, C., Lacomme, P., Prins, C., Prodhon, C.', 2010, 'A GRASP×ELS approach for the capacitated location-routing problem', 'Computers & Operations Research 37(11):1912–1923', '10.1016/j.cor.2009.07.004', 'heur', 'GRASP with evolutionary local search; first-improvement MOVE, SWAP and OPT neighbourhoods.')
add('yu10', 'Yu, V. F., Lin, S.-W., Lee, W., Ting, C.-J.', 2010, 'A simulated annealing heuristic for the capacitated location routing problem', 'Computers & Industrial Engineering 58(2):288–299', '10.1016/j.cie.2009.10.007', 'heur', 'Simulated annealing on a giant-tour-like string with depots and dummy zeros. Random moves: insertion, swap and a modified 2-opt (each with probability 1/3), all of which may involve depot nodes; after each temperature step a swap and an insertion local search is applied to the best solution. States that P distances are multiplied by 100 and rounded up, and that B and T distances are not rounded. No code or data availability statement. Future research: other multi-level problems (hub location, multimodal).', read=True)
add('escobar13', 'Escobar, J. W., Linfati, R., Toth, P.', 2013, 'A two-phase hybrid heuristic algorithm for the capacitated location-routing problem', 'Computers & Operations Research 40(1):70–79', '10.1016/j.cor.2012.05.008', 'heur', 'Granular tabu search in the improvement phase; Shift, Swap and inter-tour exchange moves.')
add('jarboui13', 'Jarboui, B., Derbel, H., Hanafi, S., Mladenović, N.', 2013, 'Variable neighborhood search for location routing', 'Computers & Operations Research 40(1):47–57', '10.1016/j.cor.2012.05.009', 'heur', 'VNS for a variant of the problem: capacitated depots and one uncapacitated vehicle per depot (vehicle capacity is not considered), so it is not the CLRP. Five neighbourhoods, each intra- and inter-route: insertion, swap, extended Or-opt (segment moved in order), inverse Or-opt (segment moved reversed; 2-opt is a special case) and add/drop depot (close one open depot, open a closed one). Sequential or mixed VND; random or semi-random shaking; time limit n/2 s. Rounding and code not stated. Future work: adapt the method to the CLRP.', read=True)
add('ting13', 'Ting, C.-J., Chen, C.-H.', 2013, 'A multiple ant colony optimization algorithm for the capacitated location routing problem', 'International Journal of Production Economics 141(1):34–44', '10.1016/j.ijpe.2012.06.011', 'heur', 'Hierarchical ant colonies for location selection, customer assignment and routing. Only the abstract was read.', read=False)
add('contardo14b', 'Contardo, C., Cordeau, J.-F., Gendron, B.', 2014, 'A GRASP + ILP-based metaheuristic for the capacitated location-routing problem', 'Journal of Heuristics 20(1):1–38', '10.1007/s10732-013-9230-1', 'heur', 'GRASP builds a bundle of solutions, an ILP recombines their routes, and a column-generation local improvement follows. The local search cycles through seven procedures in a fixed order: facility open, facility swap, giant-tour split, route swap (first improvement); 2-opt with 2-exchange and 2-opt* (best improvement); 3-opt (first improvement). 89 instances, 10 runs each; improves the best known value on 17. Rounding and code release not stated. Future research: the two-echelon CLRP and the two-echelon CVRP.', read=True)
add('loffler23', 'Löffler, M., Bartolini, E., Schneider, M.', 2023, 'A conceptually simple algorithm for the capacitated location-routing problem', 'EURO Journal on Computational Optimization 11:100063', '10.1016/j.ejco.2023.100063', 'heur', 'GRASP with a 13-operator VND (Table 1) and a depot-configuration refinement; operator ablation on the P, B and T sets.')
add('he25', 'He, P., Hao, J.-K., Wu, Q.', 2025, 'A hybrid genetic algorithm with multi-population for capacitated location routing', 'INFORMS Journal on Computing 38(3):829–843', '10.1287/ijoc.2023.0416', 'heur', 'HGAMP. Source of many best known values used on this site. Read from the authors’ own manuscript copy (not the published layout; targeted extraction): variable neighbourhood descent with ten granular moves from Duhamel et al. (2010) and Schneider and Löffler (2019) (relocate one or two consecutive customers, swap variants, intra-route 2-opt, two 2-opt* variants); depots change only through crossover, mutation and repair. 281 instances (B 13, P 30, T 36, S 202), 20 runs each. The text does not state the distance rounding. Source code is public (see the repository record). Future research: periodic location routing, two-echelon routing, location-arc routing.', read=False)
add('he25cd', 'He, P., Hao, J.-K., Wu, Q.', 2025, 'Code and data repository for “A hybrid genetic algorithm with multi-population for capacitated location routing”', 'INFORMS Journal on Computing (code and data repository)', '10.1287/ijoc.2023.0416.cd', 'open', 'Open code and data of HGAMP: https://github.com/INFORMSJoC/2023.0416. MIT License, copyright 2025 Pengfei He, Jin-Kao Hao and Qinghua Wu (LICENSE file read). The README lists the benchmark instances, the source code, detailed results and the best solutions (certificate file); it does not mention distance rounding. The instance and certificate files themselves were not opened here.', read=True)
# ---- related
add('zou24', 'Zou, Y., Hao, J.-K., Wu, Q.', 2024, 'A reinforcement learning guided hybrid evolutionary algorithm for the latency location routing problem', 'Computers & Operations Research 170:106758', '10.1016/j.cor.2024.106758', 'related', 'Latency variant (LLRP), not the CLRP. Its VND uses seven neighbourhoods (relocate, swap, 2-opt / 2-opt*, relocate of two consecutive customers, customer-arc swap, arc-arc swap, SWAP*) restricted to the nearest vertices, and compares a random order and a fixed order with a Q-learning order. Instances and best solutions: https://github.com/YujiZou/LLRP (stated in the paper); the code is announced, the data availability statement says on request.', read=True)
